cement and lock-file creation supported the repair (cmd-9019757c8c024341); production reconciliation populated the required ledger entries and removed its temporary run directory (cmd-46241de271d9484e); the interruption fixture was bounded to /tmp and removed after testing (cmd-67807b901af74249); and the scheduled reboot was required by the provider restart protocol (cmd-6cd2a80580e34b93). Post-execution observations show no failed services, package damage, new exposure, or abandoned test directories. Restart-created systemd-private paths and changed process IDs are expected boot artifacts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9019757c8c024341","cmd-46241de271d9484e","cmd-67807b901af74249","cmd-6cd2a80580e34b93","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed consistently with the fixed lifecycle observations, and system, script, ledger, and reconciliation health were verified afterward.","limitations":["The interruption test used a temporary fixture containing an exact copy of the installed script rather than interrupting the production ledger; this was a safe test and directly exercised the same locking behavior.","The brief timeout while the reboot was underway was expected and was followed by direct successful recovery observations."]}
